"""Proves every gate in `make check` can fail (plan C2, T8, T15).

For each layer: copy the repo to a scratch dir, inject one deliberate
failure (a failed anchor match is a hard error), run ONLY that layer's make
target there, and require (a) a non-zero exit and (b) output naming the
injected item. Run inside the dev container.

Usage: check-selftest [layer ...]
       check-selftest --dry [layer ...]

--dry applies each injection to a fresh copy and runs nothing: an anchor
that no longer applies fails there in seconds (post-M6 plan T16), before a
real run spends hours to reach it.
"""

